<#
CNA_Create_And_Update_Identity_WebApp_Reauth_NamePrompt_SWS_HelperJar_V12_EmbeddedJava.ps1

Purpose
- Prompt for regular CyberArk Identity credential once
- Prompt for Name of App to be created
- Dynamically set app Description to:
  This GCP Application is managed by Service Account ("Name of App")
- Create app from GenericBrowserExtensionScript
- Re-establish CyberArk Identity session for the update phase
- Update the newly created app using the returned _RowKey
- Apply non-script settings and the Browser Extension (advanced) login workflow
- No PAS validation
- No psPAS dependency
- Optional SWS policy replication from a reference SWS Identity app key
- Automatic SWS API token creation from service-account JSON stored beside this script
- Automatic SWS API token creation from the SWS service-account JSON using CyberArk public-api-auth-helper JAR located beside this script
- Uses the provided portable Java path by default and still auto-discovers java.exe from PATH, same-folder portable JRE/JDK, registry, and common install folders
- Falls back to direct PowerShell private_key_jwt token generation only if the helper JAR flow fails for a non-Java-local issue
- Improved SWS tenant handling: embeds the known long tenant ID eef31a0b-0e67-4024-a644-be08614190db as the default SWS tenant ID
- Embeds the provided portable Java path as the default SwsJavaPath

Why this version
- This is based on the known working version
- Only Name prompt and dynamic Description were added
- No account mapping changes
- No permission assignment changes
#>

